course: dictionary
lesson: 15794
title: Everyone agrees: unanimous
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When a group votes, the word unanimous tells you that everyone chose the same thing. «The class vote for the school trip was unanimous.» The clues are vote and class. Unanimous must mean that every single person agreed.
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence: «The class vote for the school trip was everyone agreed.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If even one child had voted differently, the vote would not be unanimous.
explain: Writers also use unanimous to describe people, not just votes. «The judges were unanimous in their praise for the singer.» Here it means all the judges agreed that the singer was good. The clue is praise, so it is about what people said.
fact: Unanimous means everyone in the group agrees, with nobody against.
fact: «A unanimous vote» means every person voted the same way.
fact: Unanimous is used for votes in class, councils, juries, courts and clubs.
fact: «Unanimous in their praise» means everyone said good things.
fact: Unanimous is not compared, so you cannot say «more unanimous».
exercise: «The club members were unanimous in their praise for the new park.» What does unanimous show? | They were all tired | *Everyone agreed, with nobody against | They wanted to leave early | Only a few people liked it
exercise: «The jury gave a unanimous decision: all twelve people said the man was innocent.» What does unanimous mean here? | The judge was angry | *Every juror agreed | Nobody came to court | Some people disagreed
exercise: Find the word that means everyone agreed in «The vote was unanimous, so the class went to the museum.» | museum | vote | class | *unanimous
test: «The council vote was unanimous: all ten members raised their hands.» How many members agreed? | Nine | *Ten | Some | None
test: Which sentence shows a unanimous decision? | *Every child in the club voted for the beach | Some children wanted the beach and others the park | Three voters said yes and two said no | Most people liked the idea but Sam did not
exam: In a class vote, all 24 children chose the same day trip. Which word describes this vote? | *Unanimous | Ancient | Mid | Barely
